# ---- Data and artefacts
#
# data/raw/ is COMMITTED on purpose. The source dataset is Open Database
# License (ODbL), which permits redistribution with attribution, and the file
# is ~1 MB. Committing it makes the project reproducible and lets Streamlit
# Community Cloud rebuild the model without Kaggle credentials.
#
# Derived files are regenerable, so they stay out of git:
data/processed/

# models/ IS committed (see README): Streamlit Community Cloud installs
# requirements and runs app.py, but does not run the training script, so the
# deployed app needs the artefacts present in the repository.
# If you would rather not commit a ~31 MB model, uncomment these two lines and
# train on the host instead:
# models/*.joblib
# models/*.json
